{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1387911-infusion-rebuild","id":1387911,"title":"Infusion Rebuild","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-12T22:34:36-07:00","id":1387911,"title":"Infusion Rebuild","content":"Infusion has always been a bit of a odd duck as an art, existing pretty much purely to give Nockers tech in previous editions, something the much less technophobic 20th edition made rather unnecissary fixing problems that no longer existed and not engaging properly with either the arts system or the crafting system. Which is too bad since the idea of Magical crafting powers does have alot of thematic cache so its worth having as an idea..<br /> <br /> That being said lets rebuild it.. make it something worth working with<br /> <br /> I'm going to start from the top. The ultimate power of the art(not counting theoretical legendary applications.. which is a matter for a different thread)<br /> <br /> <br /> So what should the greatest acts of creation that are generally replicatable be able to do? I'm going to look at Lycians here. It works with the idea of &quot;Infusion&quot; works across multiple realms rather than limiting it to Fae 5 only and is a unique thing that exists outside the current crafting system. <br /> <br /> Cogs also exist outside this system!I So something that allows the creation of Renegade Cogs and Lycians. Since version one was named Gilgul we can argue its not about &quot;creation&quot; per se but drawing them from wherever. So.. lets add a little more utility if rare the transition of Inanimae between Anchors.<br /> <br /> Ok!<br /> <br /> So how easy should it be to do? My first thought is requiring permanent glamour or wp to use but that seems to even more fully put it in the fiat category. My second thought is to make it us temporary tempers but require them at the beginning of the process, building things even for a boggan takes time so they won't be mass producing killbots.. but i'm not quite happy with that either. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T00:35:56-07:00","id":1387945,"title":"","content":"I'm not to the end of the Player's Guide since I just started reading the book from cover to cover, but in my initial look through I was disappointed that Infusion didn't seem to follow the principles of Art Design found in the core C20 book, it had so much potential, and as you said it doesn't seem to engage with the system of Crafting. Cantrips shouldn't just work with only one Realm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T18:02:12-07:00","id":1388201,"title":"","content":"IT violates a bunch of ideas, cantrips shouldn't work with one realm. Cantrips shouldn't be &quot;this level but better!&quot; so the lower level is a speed bump.<br /> <br /> But I Feel creating Lycians and potentially Renegade Cogs(by stealing bodies!) has some neat potential there is suitably epic for a level 5 power even its in the more &quot;Spring 5 temporary resurection&quot; Trick than something you'd use fairly often... <br /> <br /> It also covers a Variety of options, though it may need to return Scene its older variant rather than a metarealm.. but not every realm works super well with every art.. this covers nature, prop, actor, fae is abit of a difficult one to push rather than the meta-only but creating from the works of fairies and other supernaturals might work..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T14:02:36-07:00","id":1388425,"title":"","content":"It would be interesting if creation on the level of making Lycians or Cogs run a greater risk of gaining Nightmare/Bedlam. That power on that level can drive a creator mad, MAD I SAY!<br /> <br /> I like the idea of Infusion being able to &quot;pour&quot; a chimerical nature into the target of any Realm. Perhaps creating a Chimerical aspect that can be shaped or even harvested. Such as using actor to attach a chimerical &quot;fuse box&quot; to a troublesome mortal, so as to better make mortal servitors, slaves and minions.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":1756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","user":"MythAdvocate","date":". 05-14-2020, 05:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T15:30:47-07:00","id":1388459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1387911-infusion-rebuild?p=1387945#post1387945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not to the end of the Player's Guide since I just started reading the book from cover to cover, but in my initial look through I was disappointed that Infusion didn't seem to follow the principles of Art Design found in the core C20 book, it had so much potential, and as you said it doesn't seem to engage with the system of Crafting. Cantrips shouldn't just work with only one Realm.</div> </div> </div> </div>...didn't they fix that in the errata phase, to the point that Infusion in the final version is completely different from the one in the Advanced Copy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T16:11:29-07:00","id":1388474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythAdvocate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1387911-infusion-rebuild?p=1388425#post1388425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would be interesting if creation on the level of making Lycians or Cogs run a greater risk of gaining Nightmare/Bedlam. That power on that level can drive a creator mad, MAD I SAY!<br /> <br /> I like the idea of Infusion being able to &quot;pour&quot; a chimerical nature into the target of any Realm. Perhaps creating a Chimerical aspect that can be shaped or even harvested. Such as using actor to attach a chimerical &quot;fuse box&quot; to a troublesome mortal, so as to better make mortal servitors, slaves and minions.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Or rip out their soul and replace it with a superior crafting of glamour! But automatic Nightmare is a neat idea that will keep someone from making alot.. and those who do are a story in and of themselves...<br /> <br /> Hmmm this add some ideas... Maybe Mechorgs are a dirty little secret of the art something generally benign twist... but how to fit it..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T16:35:31-07:00","id":1388480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1387911-infusion-rebuild?p=1388474#post1388474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Or rip out their soul and replace it with a superior crafting of glamour! But automatic Nightmare is a neat idea that will keep someone from making alot.. and those who do are a story in and of themselves...<br /> <br /> Hmmm this add some ideas... Maybe Mechorgs are a dirty little secret of the art something generally benign twist... but how to fit it..</div> </div> </div> </div>A bit of dreadful backstory in my games was a process by which wicked Sidhe would steal mortal children to reincarnate into. This was done via a ritual similar to the changeling way, but could work here.<br /> <br /> The classic fairy tale trope of removing ones &quot;heart&quot; comes to mind here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-15T12:23:03-07:00","id":1388733,"title":"","content":"SO I really like the idea that the cost is madness. This works really well with the whole Mad scientist trope. Keeps Pcs to a reasonable level and lets you have a Lost one Freehold full of killbots.<br /> <br /> <br /> So... lets call it.. Gilgul: Calling down the Divine Fire","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T06:49:24-07:00","id":1388916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1387911-infusion-rebuild?p=1388459#post1388459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...didn't they fix that in the errata phase, to the point that Infusion in the final version is completely different from the one in the Advanced Copy?</div> </div> </div> </div>They did, mostly. It has its own issues though. <br /> Energized was reworked to let you create &quot;batteries&quot; of Glamour, up to your rating in Glamour, with the warning that &quot;carrying them could lead to Bedlam&quot;, without any mechanics behind it, ahem.<br /> <br /> You would think having an Art that could provide electromotive force to objects or people would be useful, butttttt...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25625-magicjuggler","name":"MagicJuggler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25625_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-16T06:55:06-07:00","id":1388921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MagicJuggler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1387911-infusion-rebuild?p=1388916#post1388916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They did, mostly. It has its own issues though.<br /> Energized was reworked to let you create &quot;batteries&quot; of Glamour, up to your rating in Glamour, with the warning that &quot;carrying them could lead to Bedlam&quot;, without any mechanics behind it, ahem.<br /> <br /> You would think having an Art that could provide electromotive force to objects or people would be useful, butttttt...</div> </div> </div> </div>I miss the Gematria discussion brought up in Knockers, it really added a lot to the mysticism of crafters and enchanters of Treasures. <br /> <br /> <br /> When I finish reading the Players Guide I may take a crack at Patching Infusion before I move to patching the Slivers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T08:47:46-07:00","id":1390788,"title":"","content":"So I have been rethinking this again; Infusion as an art was built before Unleashing was a thing. Maybe the Creation of True Life cannot be made into an art level.. but REQUIRES the Chaos of Unleashing?<br /> <br /> I am not really sure about this though...it feels off","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T03:18:39-07:00","id":1390944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1387911-infusion-rebuild?p=1390788#post1390788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I have been rethinking this again; Infusion as an art was built before Unleashing was a thing. Maybe the Creation of True Life cannot be made into an art level.. but REQUIRES the Chaos of Unleashing?<br /> <br /> I am not really sure about this though...it feels off</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean it fits for me. before we got Infusion as returning, I had it things like Renegade Cogs and the Werpintingle were made into true Fae Souls with essentially lucky Unleashings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T20:16:38-07:00","id":1391114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1387911-infusion-rebuild?p=1388921#post1388921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I miss the Gematria discussion brought up in Knockers, it really added a lot to the mysticism of crafters and enchanters of Treasures. <br /> <br /> <br /> When I finish reading the Players Guide I may take a crack at Patching Infusion before I move to patching the Slivers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I am better with it being more scientific rather than involving Gematria. Controversial, I know but the kabbalistic adjacency with Nockerspeak and the &quot;funny Jewish&quot; stereotype gets a bit uncomfortable. I know, White Wolf and &quot;magical appropriation&quot; and all but...mysticism has its place in the Crystal Circle.<br /> <br /> I imagine Infusion could, like Contracts, serve as a meta-art w means to circumvent laws of the Dreaming. Each level allows you to handle a different aspect of crafting normally barred by Chimerical crafting rules, starting from allowing 'independent power' to allowing fuller integration of mundane/chimerical reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25625,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25625-magicjuggler","user":"MagicJuggler","date":". 05-23-2020, 11:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25625-magicjuggler","name":"MagicJuggler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25625_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T07:58:56-07:00","id":1391195,"title":"","content":"The idea of it as a meta art reinspires me and covers something I've been having a problem with. I've been having with trying to figure out how to make a bag of holding.<br /> <br /> <br /> So! <br /> <br /> Infusion is the art of infusing one thing with another. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This gives us as a list of things: Glamour batteries. Mechorgs, Lycanthians, and Rogue and ot so rogue Cogs. IT may be helpful in krofting Inanimae. <br /> <br /> So two new abilities based on meta mechanics.<br /> <br /> Temporary use magic items-This seems like it could cut into the time realm, along with contracts. how to make it unique and worth getting all.<br /> <br /> Combining Arts-This has an issue of making Fae the only realm that matters so I'm not sure how to make this work out.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T14:57:47-07:00","id":1391270,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s certainly one way of refocusing it.<br /> <br /> It doesn\u2019t have to use Fae, it could still be the realm determines what you infuse, say you use nature to make a tree a Lycian or just a tree with a Fae seeming, or prop to making a flaming sword by either tying an art or a chimera to it. Inspiration can be drawn from both Werewolf fetishes and Mummy relics ( they bind relic items into different physical items like a I don\u2019t know a relic torch into a physical bag so the bag can hold light).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T20:06:32-07:00","id":1391408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1387911-infusion-rebuild?p=1391270#post1391270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s certainly one way of refocusing it.<br /> <br /> It doesn\u2019t have to use Fae, it could still be the realm determines what you infuse, say you use nature to make a tree a Lycian or just a tree with a Fae seeming, or prop to making a flaming sword by either tying an art or a chimera to it. Inspiration can be drawn from both Werewolf fetishes and Mummy relics ( they bind relic items into different physical items like a I don\u2019t know a relic torch into a physical bag so the bag can hold light).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There's already methods for making permanent Treasures. I was thinking an effect that lets me infuse an art in an art Basically make a combo Art. But that seems extremely limited. So I am not sure about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T21:09:43-07:00","id":1391415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1387911-infusion-rebuild?p=1391408#post1391408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> There's already methods for making permanent Treasures. I was thinking an effect that lets me infuse an art in an art Basically make a combo Art. But that seems extremely limited. So I am not sure about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well we can already infuse arts with arts using Fae 5.<br /> <br /> And I don\u2019t know if I would consider renegade cogs Treasures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T18:03:38-07:00","id":1391818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1387911-infusion-rebuild?p=1391415#post1391415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well we can already infuse arts with arts using Fae 5.<br /> <br /> And I don\u2019t know if I would consider renegade cogs Treasures.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> We can cast arts on arts with fae 5. We can't make something that is a &quot;combo&quot; effect... like say making a bag that's bigger on the inside.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T11:17:38-07:00","id":1392852,"title":"","content":"I would actually propose players look at Charlie Cantrell's conversion guide, which eliminates the Fae realm wholesale. The system makes the line between chimerical reality and the &quot;real&quot; world much less concrete, and one mechanical reflection is that basically, Realms no longer care whether something is chimerical or not. A magic sword is still a sword (and therefore a prop). A changeling is still a person (and therefore an actor). Given that Infusion always seems to only give a crap about Fae, the central question I would ask is &quot;what would infusion look like if it was entirely unable to use the Fae realm?&quot;<br /> <br /> Funnily enough, rereading the Prop write up, Prop would work with basically any Realm provided Fae didn't exist. If you want to use Maker's eye to check out a chimerical wolf, you would need Nature. If you wanted to alter a Chimerical sword, you would need Prop. Once you remove Fae entirely, the Art becomes far more functionally diverse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25663-rigelj","name":"RigelJ","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-30T15:35:43-07:00","id":1392922,"title":"","content":"You've just basically moved it to prop? <br /> <br /> It would also still have the following problems:<br /> <br /> Level 1. is still increadibly niche. Though its in a better place than it is now.<br /> <br /> Level 2 and 4 are the same damned thing but &quot;better&quot;<br /> <br /> 5 is still... in an extremely dubious place<br /> <br /> 3 isn't really effected by Fae not existing asside from the fact that I'd need to know people's names to charge them rather than &quot;HEY YOU LEPRECHAUN&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-11T12:56:10-07:00","id":1395890,"title":"","content":"I just read the infusion part of the book in my full read through, yeah I\u2019ll definitely rewrite when I get the time. What was the original version released in C20?<br /> <br /> Honestly I feel making Chimera would be possible without dedicating a Cantrip to it so it\u2019s a bit of a. air Breathing Mermaid problem. It feels having a cantrips should allow more options or enhance your abilities in making Chimera rather then being the sole source of your capacity to do so. Not to mention Unleashings of all kinds should allow Chimera Creation. And making Batteries is underwhelming when we already have Dross which you can carry and spend. And it seems a little banal to reduce treasures to just dissolvable treasure points that make them all interchangeable.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m also not going to limit it to one Realm it seems unnecessary, after all Primal isn\u2019t limited to only nature. Like for instance you could have a cantrip to convert Autumn world things into Chimera, wouldn\u2019t be Fae only it would be use Nature to make a Dog into a Chimera or Prop to make a item ect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-13T15:21:52-07:00","id":1396217,"title":"","content":"Making chimera is already a thing. The battery has alot of uses: First it gives you options for storing glamour than dross doesn't allow. That in and of itself is pretty useful. Whether its hiding it, incorporating stuff into a treasure or and here's a super useful effect recharging the enchantment on an effect. This is before you get cool options like using dogs to bite people into enchantment.. or hit them with a truck and enchant them and send them into the dreaming.. charging random things with glamour is.. useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-29T08:18:49-07:00","id":1415978,"title":"","content":"So after extened thought here's my new Infusion.<br /> <br /> 1-I'm going to move to &quot;how things work&quot; as a power.. you let call it the &quot;Scouter&quot; power. I may not understand the answers I get but I can look at someone who's a werewolf and know &quot;I don't want to fight that guy&quot;<br /> <br /> 2. Fixit GOD DAMN IT!-.Lets you repair shit, and people. Nocker surgeon GO!<br /> <br /> 3. Recharge-this allows you to create glamour batteries. but also recharge things that run on glamour...like say enchantments. It can also be used offensively to drain glamour<br /> <br /> 4. Modify-functions as current level 4 may be used on any creature of the dreaming.<br /> <br /> 5. Tranmutation: The two become one. This allows you to infuse one thing into another. Make temporary magical items, make cyberware.. reenact the saddest part of Full Metal Alchemist. Will use a cost on par with Geass.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}